## Summary

**Commit `6926a5eb7c37895b50294682b51947af82194caa`** — `0270 dsv41: TF_DS_PROMPT_PICKS_ONCE (off by default): prompt attention pads its picks once per selection`, one commit on `kernel-0270` (base `27baa93`), working tree clean.

**What it does:** `prompt.zig`'s attention reuses the padded pick list (`cidx → cidxp`, −1 to whole 16-column tiles) across layers sharing an indexer selection instead of re-running the fill + copy per layer. Re-pad triggers: indexer output, a replay cut that moves rows, a new chunk (all `Tracker.stale()` hooks), with an exact `(rows, kk)` match required for reuse. Host-structure validity only; banner logs once at first reuse.

**Premise held:** layers 2–7 share 63 picks on a cold 127-token prompt exactly as the brief claims (5 fills + 5 copies saved there); the rule covers the whole chunk — **38 fills + 38 copy launches → 8 + 8 per rank per chunk**. Prefill is not graph-captured (capture sites are decode-only) — contract question answered in the report.

**Gate (all pass):** `zig build test` 27/27, 511/511, exit 0 · CUDA syntax: round-local stubs `ok` (shared stubs fail on the pristine base — known drift; no `.cu` in this patch) · harness `h0270/` 10/10 with the full case matrix (cold prompt, multi-chunk × slices, replay cut incl. hook-only and rows-key cases, pick sweep 1..64 + >64, hand corner table), every read byte-equal to an independent reference, plus 3 negative controls proving the checks aren't vacuous.

**Reviews:** two independent reviewer subagents, both VERDICT: OK, no S1. Both hit provider 500s mid-review and were revived to completion (noted in the report). All S2s fixed (dead `Tracker` default in `Chunk.init`; build.sh drift-guard gap) and the cheap S3s (independent tile width, hand corner table, `TF_DS_REPLAY_FLOOR=0` row).

**Report:** `runs/kernel-round-20261122c/report-0270.md` (real hash, launch-count table, gate results, design decisions, hardware-gate-only gaps: banner count + exact-panel bit-compare + fill/copy count profile).

**Left open / risks to know:** the saving is host launch overhead on prefill only (60 ops/chunk — expect within-noise wall time; price by launch count at the hardware gate); `tri.decode_rows` is a mutable global so pad counts can vary mid-chunk (bytes unaffected); the switch is outside the pair-switch handshake (byte-safe, but set alike on both ranks by convention).
